at the start of russia's invasion of  ukraine all predictions pointed towards  the same thing after the ballistic  missile barrage on airports and military  positions the russian air force will  quickly swoop in destroy the remaining  ukrainian air force and air defenses and  establish full superiority in the air  however 18 days into the war russia  still hasn't achieved their superiority  in fact they aren't even close to it on  top of that just their visually  confirmed losses add up to 12 planes 6  uavs and 15 helicopters i repeat these  are just the visually confirmed ones the  real numbers are higher meanwhile  according to u.s officials 80 percent of  ukraine's fixed-wing assets are still  intact and ukrainian air defenses are  still shooting down planes helicopters  and missiles ukrainian air forces and  air defenses aren't only surviving but  succeeding against the russian air force  which is 10 times their size so what's  going on here how is this even possible  ukrainians don't have flying tractors  after all here are the main reasons for  the russian air force's spectacular  failure number one smart ukrainian  maneuvering ukrainians have been  shuffling their assets around in a very  effective manner ever since the start of  the war this is why the russians initial  rocket barrage didn't break them and is  a major factor in the russian air force  being virtually ineffective against them  all this relates to reason number two  terrible russian equipment or the lack  thereof there are pictures floating  around defense blogs showing russian  pilots in jets above syria using  commercial gps units in the cockpit  things like this are a huge red flag  indicating massive problems with russian  equipment even prior to ukraine's  invasion not only that but ukrainians  also recovered pieces of paper from  downed russian jets with strike  coordinates written on them that's right  russian pilots are given pieces of paper  before takeoff but when they get there  ukrainians will have moved away already  and the pilot has nothing to strike and  then some of them get shot down by  ukrainian air defenses and so reason  number three is the lack of proper  training for pilots russian pilots fly  far less than nato pilots half as much  in fact and don't practice any complex  maneuvers beyond flying in pairs and  hitting the occasional ground targets  this is what they did in syria as well  but what works against rebel militias  won't work against a modern mechanized  opponent with proper air defenses this  relates to reason number 4 russian  inability to organize on a large scale  to establish dominance over the  ukrainian sky russians would need very  complex massive air maneuvers  coordinating a large number of aircraft  at the same time and they are just not  able to do that russians don't have the  experience or the knowledge to pull off  such actions instead they do the same  thing in the air as they do on the  ground in lieu of proper planning and  organization they just throw more  soldiers and equipment at the problem  hoping the ukrainians will eventually  buckle but it seems like this will not  happen consequently the ukrainians are  able to hold off the russians and cause  significant losses this is why russians  don't have their superiority after 18  days and most likely won't be able to  achieve it period now some people might  come in and say not so fast the russians  must be saving their strength for the  real air campaign which is definitely  coming operation godot is imminent where  the ukrainians will get wiped out we've  all heard people saying this but this is  a bad assessment as a rule of thumb if  russia could have established their  superiority they would have done so  already but they cannot so they did not  due to reasons detail in this video i  hope this little blurb from me helped  people better understand the war  situation in ukraine in the meantime you  can support me on patreon if you so  choose and i thank you for watching stay  tuned for more coverage of the ukrainian  invasion in the near future and i'll be  seeing you next time
 

